+# Review 19: one freshness rule per pipeline step
+
+Source: architecture review after PRs #12 to #14, opportunity 2.
+
+## Grok Bot review (round 0)
+
+Diff c237bc3. `pipeline/freshness.ts` replaces `pipeline/cache.ts`: each step
+compares the fingerprint of its real input with the key its last run
+recorded, through one `decide(force, recorded, current)`. Classify keeps an
+old resplit record only when it still describes the scenes it wrote. A
+`--dry-run` flag prints reuse or redo per step with no clients, keys, writes
+or network. The Muse implementation session was killed by SIGTERM from
+outside after about 5 minutes (agent-logs/19-impl-aborted.jsonl); a
+continue session finished it (19-continue.jsonl).
+
+Verified by me:
+- `npm run build:book -- oz --dry-run` (real tsx, no keys in env): segment,
+  classify, resplit and cluster all print `reuse (inputs unchanged)`.
+  `--step classify --force --dry-run` prints `redo (forced)`.
+- Oz stamp: comparing the old and new parsed analysis.json and
+  music-clusters.json, the only differences are the added
+  `provenance.input`, `provenance.resplit.input` and cluster
+  `provenance.input`. scenes.json and book.json are unchanged; files stay
+  single-line JSON with a trailing newline. 151 scenes.
+- The bug sequence is covered: forced segment then unforced classify redoes;
+  classify drops the stale resplit record; resplit then redoes and is a
+  fixed point on its own output; a full unforced rerun with throwing fake
+  clients reuses every step.
+
+1. Must: the classify and resplit keys leave out the book text. Classify
+   sends paragraph text to Jev and resplit counts words and builds windows
+   from it, but their fingerprints only cover scene fields. After
+   `ingest --force` with corrected text, a segment that comes back with the
+   same boundaries and titles would let classify and resplit reuse
+   analysis of the old text. Fix: include `book.textVersion` in the classify
+   and resplit fingerprints, re-stamp the Oz data the same way (only those
+   two values may change), update the docs table.
+2. Note, accepted: resplit keys on ranges only, so a forced classify over
+   already-split scenes keeps the resplit result instead of re-judging
+   splits with the new vectors. That is the intended behaviour: it avoids a
+   paid re-run when only emotions moved, and `--step resplit --force` stays
+   available.
+
+Checks: 306 tests, typecheck, check:isolation, check:secrets, test:hooks,
+check:size.
+Verdict: changes needed (item 1), one Muse review and fix round.
